# Project Architecture

## Folder structure

- `config/` — app-specific configuration (investment rates, targets, projections). Suffix: `.config.ts`
- `src/utils/` — pure, reusable functions (no React). Suffix: `.util.ts`
- `src/hooks/` — custom React hooks grouped by logical domain. Suffix: `.hooks.ts`
- `src/contexts/` — React Context providers + consumer hooks. Suffix: `Context.tsx`
- `src/@types/` — shared TypeScript interfaces, one file per domain (`investment.ts`, `bumba.ts`, `baloise.ts`)

## Components

Where a component lives is decided by how many pages use it, not by its size.

- `src/components/atoms/` — genuinely shared primitives used across pages (DetailCard, PageHeader, ThemeToggle, YearSelector)
- `src/components/organisms/` — shared app chrome (AppBar, BottomNav)
- `src/pages/{page}/{Page}.tsx` — top-level page components, lazy-loaded via `React.lazy()` with a `Suspense` fallback
- `src/pages/{page}/_components/{kebab-case}/{PascalCase}.tsx` — anything used by only one page (SummaryCards, BumbaTable, BaloiseFundPosition)

Page-specific components nest the same way when they grow: `bumba-table/_components/month-row/MonthRow.tsx`.

Only promote a component out of `_components/` once a second page actually needs it.

## Co-located files

Files that serve exactly one component live next to it, named after the folder:

- `{kebab-name}.util.ts` — presentation helpers (`bumba-table.util.ts`)
- `{kebab-name}.types.ts` — types used only by that component
- `{kebab-name}.constants.ts` — constants used only by that component
- `{PascalName}.styles.ts` — `cva` variants

Domain calculations stay in `src/utils/`, and domain types in `src/@types/`, even when only one component renders them today.

## Key rules

- No `.find()` or `.filter()` calls in components — extract to utils or hooks
- No data transformation in components — put it in a hook or util and let the component render the result
- No prop drilling — use Context + custom hooks for shared state
- No magic numbers — use named constants from `config/investment.config.ts`
